#X text 20 4700 PARAMETER PICKUP -- WHAT IT IS AND WHY. mother replays knobs.txt at boot so the patch believes a knob sits where the knob physically does not \, and the first touch JUMPS -- measured at 443 BPM on knob 1 \, which is master tempo. Nothing on the instrument can detect it: mother reports POSITION \, not whether that position is still true. This holds a control until its value passes THROUGH the stored one. Item 236 \, and the whole model is on ref/module/map.md, f 62;
#X text 1400 4700 ⛔ THE GATE IS ON THE NAME \, NOT ON THE VALUE \, and that is not a style choice. list append above holds the value in its COLD inlet -- suppressing the value there would leave the PREVIOUS one parked and the name would still fire it. For tempo that re-sends the same BPM and looks harmless. For a knob mapped to volca-note it would fire a note on every suppressed step \, carrying a value that could have come from another surface entirely, f 62;
#X text 2800 4700 THE ORDER IS IDENTITY THEN VALUE THEN NAME \, and all of this rests on it. t l l fires its right outlet first so the name reaches the route above before list split has run \, and list split fires its REMAINDER first so the value is decided before the name asks for the lookup. The divisor already depends on the same ordering, f 62;
#X text 20 4980 ⛔ A KNOB CAN NEVER RE-SEND ITS TARGET \, AND THAT GUARANTEE LIVES IN ANOTHER FILE. m_organelle puts every knob through change -1 \, so only DISTINCT values are ever published. That is why a crossing is detected as a SIDE FLIP rather than as equality -- waiting for a value to EQUAL the target would wait forever, f 62;
#X text 1400 4980 THE BOOT WINDOW DECIDES ONLY WHETHER TO ARM. mother pushes knobs.txt ONLY IF A SAVE HAS EVER HAPPENED -- until then it logs knobs.txt: can't open. A first value inside the window is a restore and arms \; one after it is a hand on the knob and goes straight to LIVE. Without the split \, a fresh install or any deploy.sh --clean would latch a physical touch and the knob would go DEAD after one value, f 62;
#X text 2800 4980 ⚠️ BOTH BRANCHES PASS THE VALUE THROUGH \, which is the only reason a timer is tolerable here. Item 234 was two boot races that shipped silently. A window too short costs the old jump \; one too long costs a knob that needs one sweep to free it. NEITHER CAN PRODUCE SILENCE \, and silence is what made 234 expensive to find, f 62;
#X text 20 5260 THE STATE IS PER KNOB AND LIVES IN TWO ARRAYS. 0 is VIRGIN \, 1 is armed with the side not yet known \, 2 is armed ABOVE the target waiting for a fall \, 3 is armed BELOW it waiting for a rise \, 4 is LIVE. States 2 and 3 ARE the answer they wait for offset by two \, so one comparison releases both. NEITHER ARRAY IS -k: every element is 0 at load \, which is what makes 0 mean VIRGIN for free, f 62;
#X text 1400 5260 select 0 1 4 LEAVES OUTLET 2 UNCONNECTED ON PURPOSE. LIVE is the absence of work -- the gate is already open -- so there is nothing to do and no box to do it in. Same idiom as the unconnected moses outlet above, f 62;
#X text 2800 5260 ⛔ THE -1 BYPASS KEEPS EVERY OTHER CONTROL OUT OF SLOT 0. tabread CLAMPS an out-of-range index rather than erroring \, so without select -1 every fader in the rig would read and write knob 1's state -- and the rig would keep working while pickup went haywire. C-8: that reject carries the SLOT \, not a bang, f 62;
#X text 20 5540 THE GATE DEFAULTS OPEN ON EVERY param MESSAGE \, before the value has been read. Fail-open is deliberate -- a broken filter should make a control JUMP \, not make the instrument dead, f 62;
#X text 1400 5540 ⬜ A MODE CHANGE DOES NOT RE-ARM. og-knob-1 is tempo in all six modes today so it is not reachable \, but a v0.4 row could map one knob to different destinations per mode. Doing it right needs a per-mode-and-knob value memory \; doing it cheaply is WORSE than nothing \, because re-arming to the knob's last position puts the next move on the far side and suppresses until you turn back. The arrays widen 4 to 24 with one index term. ref/module/map.md, f 62;
#X text 2800 5540 THE IDENTITY ROUTE IS DUPLICATED FROM THE DIVISOR'S \, and one t a a feeds both. Four knobs is what this hardware has and that is fixed forever \, so the duplication is bounded -- but a name added to one has to be added to BOTH, f 62;
#X obj 20 1500 t f f;
