#X text 20 1720 ⛔ THE MAPPED VALUE IS WHAT THE SCREEN SHOWS \, not the raw control position. m_organelle no longer reports knobs to disp -- a 0-to-1 number where a BPM belongs is not feedback \, it is arithmetic homework \, and the param layer REPLACES the footer so the tempo vanished while you turned it. Item 238. ⬜ Only tempo does this so far \; every other destination still shows nothing until the same pattern reaches it, f 62;
#X text 20 6250 ⛔ WHILE PICKUP HOLDS \, BOTH NUMBERS GO OUT AS ONE ROW -- bpm 57 (120): the latched tempo still in force \, and where the knob is pointing. THE VALUE MUST BE A FLOAT because g_oled runs it through makefilename %g \, so the second number rides in the UNIT field \, which is a free symbol. That is why there is a makefilename (%g) here rather than a second value, f 62;
#X text 20 6420 ⛔ A HELD VALUE NEVER REACHES THE TEMPO BRANCH \, which is why this scaling exists twice. Pickup gates the control NAME \, so the lookup never runs while a knob is held. ⬜ The universal version must put the scaling WITH its destination or every one of them duplicates this again, f 52;
